From 8a2098b8e3d6e17305caa0adb3f3d9110f15cdec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:43:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tier 0: the calls' memo keys and hashes eight at a time
 (#2874)

Measuring's loop over the deferred entries took a call's key, hashed it
(a reduction and SplitMix64's finalizer, a chain of about 30 cycles) and
probed the thread's table one call at a time. It now builds eight listed
entries' keys (tier0_call_memo_key), hashes them in one vector
(tier0_call_memo_hashes, the same hash: each key's sum the neighbouring
quadwords', the 128-bit lanes' and the halves' pairs), fetches their
slots' lines, and then probes each in order (tier0_call_memo_probe).
The table's contents and the objects are the same.

A call's entry in the table goes to its place in the deferred entries'
list (Tier0Entries.call_slots), so emission's loop over that list reads
it in order instead of the entry's kind and slot.

